          "settings": {
            "editor": "<div style='text-align:center;'><div style='font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9A7B2E;'>About Twelve Scents</div></div>"
          },
          "elements": [],
          "isInner": false
        },
        {
          "id": "b3189c5",
          "elType": "widget",
          "widgetType": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Filling the empty shelves with heroes who look like our children.",
            "header_size": "h1",
            "align": "center"
          },
          "elements": [],
          "isInner": false
        },
        {
          "id": "637d03a",
          "elType": "widget",
          "widgetType": "text-editor",
          "settings": {
            "editor": "<p style='text-align:center;'>Reclaiming the shelf. Restoring the heroes. We are brown-skin owned and Scripture rooted. The heroes of the Bible were never pale. Their stories run through brown veins, and their legacies belong in the hands of brown children who see themselves reflected in every faithful act, every bold stand, every covenant kept. We do not insert brown children into Scripture&mdash;we restore them to their rightful place within it. The Bible is their inheritance. Their children deserve to know it.</p>"
          },
          "elements": [],
          "isInner": false
        }
      ],
      "isInner": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e8d60a6",
      "elType": "container",
      "settings": {
        "content_width": "boxed",
        "background_background": "classic",
        "background_color": "#F6F1E9"
      },
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "4a828b7",
          "elType": "container",
          "settings": {
            "flex_direction": "row"
          },
          "elements": [
            {
              "id": "350fd63",
